│   "summary": "This specification defines the addition of a new read-only     │
│ analytics endpoint, GET /api/stats/{code}/daily, to the existing URL         │
│ shortener service. The endpoint aggregates existing (or newly introduced, if │
│ not already present) redirect/click event data by calendar day in UTC and    │
│ returns a JSON array of {date, clicks} objects ordered most-recent-first,    │
│ returning HTTP 200 for known codes and HTTP 404 for unknown ones. The        │
│ feature is strictly additive: it must not alter any existing endpoint's      │
│ behavior, response shape, validation logic, or the rate limiter's            │
│ configuration or enforcement, and it must integrate with the existing        │
│ authentication/authorization scheme used by comparable read endpoints in the │
│ codebase.",                                                                  │
│   "functional_requirements": [                                               │
│     "FR1: The service SHALL expose a new endpoint GET                        │
│ /api/stats/{code}/daily that accepts a short code path parameter.",          │
│     "FR2: If {code} corresponds to a short code that exists (was previously  │
│ created via the shortening endpoint), the service SHALL respond with HTTP    │
│ 200 and a JSON array body.",                                                 │
│     "FR3: If {code} does not correspond to any existing short code, the      │
│ service SHALL respond with HTTP 404 and SHALL NOT include a daily-stats      │
│ array in the response body.",                                                │
│     "FR4: Each element of the returned array SHALL be a JSON object with     │
│ exactly two fields: 'date' (string, format YYYY-MM-DD) and 'clicks'          │
│ (non-negative integer).",                                                    │
│     "FR5: The 'date' value in each object SHALL represent a calendar day     │
│ boundary computed in UTC, such that a click recorded at any UTC timestamp    │
│ within [00:00:00, 23:59:59] of that date is attributed to that date.",       │
│     "FR6: The array SHALL be ordered by date descending (most recent date    │
│ first, oldest date last), with no two objects sharing the same date value.", │
│     "FR7: Only calendar days that have at least one recorded click for the   │
