│ design: {                                                                    │
│   "architecture": "The design extends the existing layered Spring Boot MVC   │
│ app (Controller -> Service -> Repository -> H2) without introducing new      │
│ frameworks. A new JPA entity ClickEvent (id, code, clicked_at UTC timestamp) │
│ is added to persist one row per successful redirect.                         │
│ UrlShortenerService.resolveAndRecordClick is extended to, in addition to its │
│ existing incrementClickCount()/save(mapping) behavior (left byte-for-byte    │
│ unchanged in return type/contract), also persist a new ClickEvent row via a  │
│ new ClickEventRepository inside the same @Transactional method \u2014 this   │
│ keeps redirect semantics (302 + Location) untouched while making per-click   │
│ timestamps durable. A new read-only method, dailyStats(code), first verifies │
│ the code exists via the existing                                             │
│ UrlMappingRepository.findByCode(...).orElseThrow(CodeNotFoundException) path │
│ (reusing the exact same not-found semantics as existing StatsController, so  │
│ 404 behavior is identical/shared), then queries ClickEventRepository with a  │
│ JPQL aggregation grouping by DATE(clicked_at) (interpreted in UTC, since     │
│ clicked_at is stored as an Instant/UTC timestamp and H2's DATE()/CAST        │
│ truncation on a UTC-stored value yields the UTC calendar day) ordered        │
│ descending, mapping results into an ordered list of DailyClickCount(date,    │
│ clicks) records with zero-click days naturally absent because the query is   │
│ driven by existing rows only (no calendar generation). A new handler method  │
│ is added onto the existing StatsController (GET /api/stats/{code}/daily),    │
│ reusing the same GlobalExceptionHandler CodeNotFoundException->404 mapping   │
│ already used by GET /api/stats/{code}, guaranteeing identical error shape.   │
│ The endpoint is deliberately not registered in ShortenRateLimitFilter's      │
│ shouldNotFilter/isRateLimited logic (which only matches POST /api/shorten),  │
│ so it passes through the filter chain untouched, exactly like the existing   │
│ GET endpoints \u2014 no filter code changes are required. Since there is no  │
│ security framework in the codebase, the new endpoint remains public,         │
│ consistent with FR11. Schema evolution for the new ClickEvent table is       │
│ handled automatically by the existing ddl-auto=update setting against        │
│ embedded H2, requiring no migration tooling change.",                        │
